This is random thinking about game balance. I
used to think reflection was too strong, now I think
it's too easy to get.

I think if you can get a character to the oracle
alive (not all that difficult of a task) you can
complete sokoban barring YA*Ds and massive boulder
follies. So reflection is much more common between
oracle and castle than ever before. This makes many
monsters almost harmless, and those that are still
dangerous would probably be more dangerous if they
never wasted their breath so to speak.

The "oR is a key ascension kit item. This frees up
a castle wish which means the late game will be
easier too. It also makes the armor/weapon/amulet
choices for the AK less interesting since it biases
towards an optimal one: "oR, GDSM, #twoweaponing,
cloak of your choice.

It's just too good a reward for the effort. The
bag of holding I don't mind since I hate inventory
management.

So solutions might include:

1. Make sokoban harder. Reduce the ways of recovering
from mistakes (no squeezing past boulders, boulders
cannot be pickaxed, 0-1 ?oE at 3rd level not 1st). Or
penalize more for mistakes (bigger luck hits). Or
reduce or remove food from sokoban making hunger a
factor. Or add nastier monsters (nasty breath weapon
monsters on the amulet level would be poetic).

2. Replace the amulet or reduce its probability
by having more reward level possibilities. Magic
marker? Wand of polymorph? Nice potions? I think there
is so much stuff just in soko laying on the floor
that most adventurers would choose to do it anyway
even without a reward at the top.

Personally I don't mind the (BoH as a reward item
since I despise inventory management as an obstacle.

What do people with longer and fuller play experience
think?

